From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek-v4.1: fuse small decode kernels around sparse attention

Default off, each behind its own switch; switch off runs the original code.
VLLM_DSV41_TOPK_RAGGED_FUSED: the 5-launch top-k ragged metadata build (lens,
zeros, two cumsums, pack) as one Triton kernel (M <= 256, integer, bitwise).
VLLM_DSV41_TOPK_RAGGED_REUSE: build it once per index source per step
(epoch-invalidated cache). VLLM_DSV4_ATTN_DIRECT_OUT: sparse attention writes
straight into the output buffer (no per-layer DtoD copy, no fake SWA-only
indptr). VLLM_DSV41_SWA_RAGGED_INPLACE: SWA ragged build in place.
VLLM_DSV41_INDEXER_Q_LUT_FUSED: indexer q LUT decode in one kernel. All
bitwise identical (tests/test_dsv41_small_kernels_gpu.py).

